// @error: an array of references is not expressible
//
// Same dropped-modifier bug as nestedFixedArray, different modifier: the parser kept only
// the inner type's name, so `[&string; 2]` silently became `[string; 2]` — an OWNED array.
// References are second-class and cannot be stored, so an array of them has no
// representation at all, and accepting the annotation promised one.
fn main() {
    var a: [&string; 2] = ["x", "y"]
    print(a[0])
}
